{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T20:42:41.312Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\nImplemented `src/cli/mcp-files.ts` with the five MCP file tools (`listFiles`, `readFile`, `writeFile`, `editFile`, `deleteFile`) and the `McpFolderSource` type, plus `tests/mcp-files.test.ts`.\n\nKey points:\n- **Reuse, not copy**: local changes resolve via `resolveRemoteChange` + `loadConfig(cwd)`; paths go through `isSafeUploadPath`; listing uses `readChangeFiles`; remote matching uses `matchesFolder`.\n- **Gate**: every path must be safe and its deepest existing part must resolve (through symlinks) inside the change folder, else `path outside the change folder: <path>` with no write. Approved/foreign changes fail with `resolveRemoteChange`'s error; a remote change with no working copy fails with `no working copy of change <change>; run the plan tool first`.\n- **Known failures** (gate, missing file, bad argument, edit count) return `isError: true` with newline-terminated text and never throw; other errors propagate to the handler.\n- Files: 240 lines (≤250), all functions under 80, tagged `@scenario cli-foundation: ...` and `@adr 014`.\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/mcp-files.test.ts` — 6/6 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify` — full typecheck, build, all tests (137 UI + CLI suites), and lint pass.\n- Budget tests (line, function, no-inert, no-skipped) pass.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/163-local-mcp/.run/results/2.md`."}}
